        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 80-year-old female admitted on 06/02/2011 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced exercise tolerance. Chest auscultation revealed widespread expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray was performed to exclude pneumonia and pneumothorax. Oxygen saturation was monitored throughout her stay. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed type 1 respiratory failure. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), a course of oral prednisolone, and controlled oxygen therapy. She responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. She was discharged on 07/02/2011 in stable condition. I recommend continuation of her inhaler regimen and close follow-up in your practice. Please do not hesitate to contact me with any questions.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
